    "title": "Lawmakers Test the Rules for AI Agents That Move Money",
    "summary": "Artificial intelligence (AI) agents, stablecoins and tokenized securities put some of the mechanics of digital finance before lawmakers Wednesday (Sept. 2), including how software-driven transactions will be authorized and settled. At a House Financial Services Committee hearing that ranged across tech-driven innovation’s role against a backdrop of financial regulation and economic policy, members of Congress […]\nThe post Lawmakers Test the Rules for AI Agents That Move Money appeared first on PYMNTS.com.",
